In article <C708Mq.BG2@volvo.volvo.se> martin@ant (Martin Borjesson) writes:
>: CDS and DNS store different information. CDS does not perform hostname/IP
>: mapping, etc. They really don't have anything in common, except as mentioned
>: earlier. CDS and DNS serve different purposes.
>
>In the pictures at page 51 and 52 in the book "Understanding DCE" they
>obviously does IP/interface mapping.... Maybe this is wrong too?
