The interface is RPC interface mapping, not network interface, if thats
what you were thinking. The whole point behind storing the RPC binding
information in CDS (also called the "interface") is so clients can find
the location of servers. The IP address is used to contact the end point
mapper which then contains the port on which the server is listening.

I can see how this could have confused you though.

Roland







