I justy gotta add my two cents....

 As our cell environments grow, we are going to need more and more management
facilities for domain management. DCE was supossed to help with this, and DME
is expected to do more. 

 The problem I see is that CDS can provide the binding for the DCE client,
but all hells gonna break loose when the network bindings (named, bind, dns,
NIS, NFS, etc) won't let the application run where it needs to.

 Anyone heard any talk about bringing all this stuff together? If not,
is DCE really worth the overhead just to get RPC's? Some people might
think the increased administration of DCE (plus NIS, DNS, and NFS already
in place) isn't worth the cost of building RPC's (and since they still have
to compile the rest of teh RPC on the target platform, any competent 
programmer can build a message passing scheme which approximates RPC's.
After all, we have been doing this already for years).

 Its gonna be hard to justify DCE to management and clients unless we 
address the management and administration issues.

