In article <C6noC9.AIs@volvo.volvo.se> martin@ant (Martin Borjesson) writes:
>Hello!
>
>How well is the connection between DCE/CDS and DNS done? I suppose that the
>basic function is when CDS can ask the DNS questions. 

I think the only interaction between CDS and DNS is during inter-cell
communication when a client needs to find a CDS server in another (DNS-named)
cell. For example, if I'm in the cell /.../stanford.edu and lookup a CDS
object in /.../mit.edu/ then the interaction is (if I recall correctly):

     Source                Question                            Destination
     -------               --------                            -----------
     client program  ->    resolv "/.../mit.edu/blah"       -> CDS clerk 
     CDS clerk       ->    where is GDA                     -> CDS server
     CDS server      ->    GDA is located at X              -> CDS clerk
     CDS clerk       ->    find CDS server in cell mit.edu  -> GDA
     GDA             ->    get me info about mit.edu        -> DNS
     DNS             ->    here is the info about mit.edu   -> GDA
     GDA             ->    here is a CDS server for mit.edu -> CDS clerk
     CDS clerk       ->    contacts CDS server at mit       -> CDS server

My DCE manuals are at home so I might have messed up something :-)

>But, can a DNS get questions answered from the CDS. Can the CDS act like 
>a full DNS server, from the DNS world?
>

No. CDS is a new name server and speaks only DCE RPC. Its not intended to
replace DNS (at this point). It would be possible to write a DNS gateway 
and store DNS information in CDS. The gateway would convert DNS requests 
to CDS requests. Not sure if anyone plans on doing it though. 

Roland

